"id":171281177,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3MTI4MTE3Nw==","user":{"login":"alexstaytuned","id":192051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjA1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned","html_url":"https://github.com/alexstaytuned","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-01-13T12:48:43Z","updated_at":"2016-01-13T12:49:25Z","body":"@normanmaurer,\n\nI also agree with @ctron that this behavior is non-intuitive and hope this issue can be revisited.\n\nAre you saying that for two-way conversion, MessageToMessageCodec<MyMessageType, ByteBuf> is recommended over ByteToMessageCodec<MyMessageType>? The latter seems more intuitive. Both are mentioned in Netty In Action as valid alternatives.\n\nAlso, by sending an empty buffer to decode, I think we are violating the integrity property that any message sent to decode has been previously sent. This is the code path sending empty buffers:\n\n```\npublic void channelInactive(ChannelHandlerContext ctx) throws Exception {\n    RecyclableArrayList out = RecyclableArrayList.newInstance();\n    try {\n        if (cumulation != null) {\n            callDecode(ctx, cumulation, out);\n            decodeLast(ctx, cumulation, out);\n        } else {\n            decodeLast(ctx, Unpooled.EMPTY_BUFFER, out);\n        }\n    ...\n```\n\nWhy is `decodeLast(ctx, Unpooled.EMPTY_BUFFER, out);` necessary here?\n\nIf we want people to not use ByteToMessageCodec due to this behavior, let's indicate so in the docs.\n\ncc @trustin who is the author of this logic.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/171281177/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"alexstaytuned","id":192051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjA1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned","html_url":"https://github.com/alexstaytuned","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexstaytuned/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":513644762,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50NTEzNjQ0NzYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/events/513644762","actor":{"login":"normanmaurer","id":439362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/439362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer","html_url":"https://github.com/normanmaurer","followers_url":"htt